# Always Refer to Project Docs

Before planning, designing, or implementing anything, read the relevant project docs and treat them as the source of truth.

## Canonical docs

| Doc | Use for |
|---|---|
| `PRD.md` | Product goals, flows, features, UX, acceptance criteria |
| `architecture (2).md` | System design, services, data flow, boundaries |
| `techstack.md` | Allowed technologies and hosting choices |

## Rules

- Prefer these docs over assumptions or generic defaults.
- If a request conflicts with the docs, call out the conflict and ask before changing direction.
- When adding or changing features, align with the PRD flow and architecture boundaries.
- Do not introduce stack choices that contradict `techstack.md` unless the user explicitly approves.
- If docs are missing detail for the task, say what is missing instead of inventing a parallel design.
